17. Rollback Strategy

This is a very important interview topic.

Define rollback before starting production migration.

Example:

                    Production Cutover
                           |
                    Application validation
                           |
                 +---------+---------+
                 |                   |
               PASS                FAIL
                 |                   |
                 v                   v
            Continue          Start rollback
                                     |
                                     v
                              Redirect traffic
                                     |
                                     v
                              Restore old system
                                     |
                                     v
                              Validate application

Rollback triggers could include:

Critical application errors
Database inconsistency
Payment transaction failures
Unexpected latency
Connectivity failures
Data synchronization issues

The exact thresholds should be agreed with application, database, business, and operations teams before the cutover.

18. RTO and RPO

Document these clearly.

RTO

Recovery Time Objective

Maximum acceptable time to restore service after a failure.

Example:

RTO = 30 minutes
RPO

Recovery Point Objective

Maximum acceptable amount of data loss measured in time.

Example:

RPO = 5 minutes

For the case study:

RTO: 30 minutes
RPO: 5 minutes

Then explain how the architecture supports those targets.

